<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Punjabi strings of the iPhone UI, in the Gurmukhi script. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the
  text shows, the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  The polite form "ਤੁਸੀਂ" with "-ੋ", and English loanwords where Punjabi iOS uses them ("ਡਿਲੀਟ").
  Punjabi has the CLDR plural forms one and other; "one" also takes 0, so each form keeps the number.
  The duration chips have no unit, because "12–24 ਘੰਟੇ" is longer than 7 characters: the captions name the hours.
-->
